---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CompositeKeyGenerator from '../../components/CompositeKeyGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="SQL Composite Primary Key Generator" description="Generate an ALTER TABLE statement adding a composite (multi-column) primary key.">
  <CompositeKeyGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>When you need more than one column as a key</h2>
  <p>A composite primary key uses two or more columns together to guarantee uniqueness — most commonly seen in many-to-many join tables, where neither column alone is unique, but the combination always is.</p>

  <h2>How to use this generator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter your table name.</li>
    <li>List the columns that together form the unique key.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated ALTER TABLE statement.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <p>For a join table linking orders and products: <code>ALTER TABLE order_items ADD PRIMARY KEY (order_id, product_id);</code> — ensuring no duplicate order/product pairing exists.</p>

  <h2>Common Composite Key Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Adding a composite key to a table that already has duplicate rows</strong> for that column combination — the ALTER statement will fail until duplicates are resolved.</li>
    <li><strong>Using a composite key where a single surrogate key (auto-increment ID) would be simpler</strong> — composite keys make foreign key references from other tables more verbose.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This Composite Key Generator</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Defining a proper key for a many-to-many join table</li>
    <li>Enforcing uniqueness across a natural combination of columns (like year + month + region)</li>
    <li>Fixing a table that was created without any primary key constraint</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Composite Primary Key FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Can I add a composite key alongside a separate unique ID column?</strong> Yes — many tables have both an auto-increment ID as primary key and a separate unique constraint on a column combination, rather than making the combination itself the primary key.</p>
</ToolLayout>
